{"agent_id":"pp3g-ndGC-read-only-post-hoc-audit-phase-2-per-workflow-ea46","agent_seq":7,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T03:43:30.934449923Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"3b8274f4-d06e-415a-b1a8-aaab3bdf6237","comment_uuid":"7fbeb8b7-fc7c-483f-b612-360e590db8de","author":"pp3g-ndGC-read-only-post-hoc-audit-phase-2-per-workflow-ea46","content":"## PHASE-2 POST-HOC AUDIT VERDICT — CONDITIONAL (2026-08-08)\n\nScope: read-only audit of committed fork-local/agents@a87bd513 against r2 boundary 7c5b3e88 (prior r2 parent 5ada263a), plus #125 process trail. No source files, code, commits, pushes, or issue closure performed.\n\n### Outcome: APPROVE\nIndependent source re-derivation finds the four r3 items integrate cleanly and preserve the r2 fail-closed boundary:\n- **R1 / HIGH confidence:**  now distinguishes absent named remote from confirmed zero remotes;  from  is Forbidden, non-empty enumeration is Forbidden, only confirmed empty is Allowed. Result helper and tests: , ; decision tests: . This closes the prior ghost-remote fail-open without weakening existing v2/v3 decisions.\n- **R2 / HIGH:**  consumes v2/v3 hydration errors into  and warns;  delegates and has no propagating error arm. The extraction preserves warn-and-continue and keeps successful hydration marker/reporting in the Hydrated arm.\n- **Item 3 / HIGH:**  pins marker write, agent-row preservation, stale-row exclusion, and second-call short-circuit on forbidden skip.\n- **R3 / HIGH mechanism, MEDIUM-HIGH end-to-end:**  performs re-emit -> one lock acquisition -> locked decision -> clear -> locked hydrate;  delegates to , avoiding the non-reentrant 30-second second-acquire hazard ().\nCommit hygiene: message is ;  clean; fork tree equals commit tree. The independently recorded verification tail reports full suites green (1813 lib / 2892 bin / 194 CLI integration / 159 smoke / 1 AC10), 13 r3 tests passing, binary  matching commit SHA, and stable 260-issue live sanity with no collision warning.\n\n### Findings (severity-ranked)\n1. **MEDIUM — systemic process reliability:** three builder stalls/silent-hangs occurred on this single r3 lifecycle: T1jj stalled after plan, neHg was position/artifact-silent and was killed, and R99p went silent after commit before final verification. The in-flight auditor cXmI caught the first two; the cadence breach during R99p verification was correctly classified as liveness-backed rather than a stall; SzyI completed the verification tail. This means the artifact outcome held, but the original builder process did not. Evidence: #125 trail 01:26–01:58, 02:33, 02:41, 03:00–03:33; Phase-1 summary 03:39. Recommendation: retain mandatory ~10-minute position heartbeats and pre-position independent verification for long builds; treat repeated silent-hang recurrence as a workflow reliability issue, not builder success.\n2. **LOW — position/claim discipline:** final SzyI result explicitly states WHY/WHAT/CERTAINTY/WHAT-NOT-TESTED per item, satisfying the claim contract (). Earlier builder positions did not consistently include all four fields, and the mid-position said 11 tests while the commit contains 13; the verifier corrected this with artifact evidence. No resulting artifact divergence, but the contract should apply at every load-bearing position, not only final result.\n3. **LOW — clean-tree qualification:** tracked fork state is clean, but the recorded tree retained untracked ; it was treated as allowed and temporarily moved for clean version embedding. This is operationally understood, but “clean tree” should be reported as “clean tracked tree; known untracked backup” or the backup should be ignored outside the audited fork.\n4. **LOW — warning assertion depth:**  () asserts the  outcome, while warning emission is only source-structurally verified at ; it does not capture a tracing record. This is adequate for the agreed no-new-infra scope and not a fail-open, but leaves logging itself unpinned.\n\n### Process compliance disposition\nPlans, checkpoints, results, issue ownership, fork commit, independent verification, and non-closure of #125 were tracked. The two-phase auditor flow worked: cXmI identified real stalls and orchestrator dispositions; SzyI independently joined commit, tests, binary, and live-sanity artifacts. Attribution of one early position was corrected in the trail rather than silently retained. Process therefore **partially held up**, with the systemic reliability finding above.\n\n### WHAT-NOT-TESTED\nNo live concurrent-kickoff race, live v2-mode integrity repair, or live daemon tick with a real dispatcher failure was run; ignored smoke tests were unchanged; no ASES-side documentation changes were audited as part of r3. Unit/source evidence supports the verdict, but those live cases remain outside demonstrated coverage.\n\n### Bottom line\n**CONDITIONAL approval:** r3 outcome is approved and has no identified architectural regression or new fail-open. Conditionality is on workflow/process reliability: address the repeated silent-hang/heartbeat pattern and tighten position claim fields before treating this task class as process-complete. #125 remains open.","created_at":"2026-08-08T03:43:30.898248228Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:hZbOEgFpZnQufd+aX844eDvHM8nhEr0QfcpOLxrNBFY","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgAC3wrZ9coeUSXA/qjR9v30Mr5arIsgNuuQfyQeqZvssAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAPaVAG1mtiJ9JKRi3P+hOxaaW9w795vfbaGRBlgoL4QeKtJUMbaTswYF7elO6tCgMfqKhsAiYcT2t2LXKi3AmCQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:hZbOEgFpZnQufd+aX844eDvHM8nhEr0QfcpOLxrNBFY","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgAC3wrZ9coeUSXA/qjR9v30Mr5arIsgNuuQfyQeqZvssAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKRpl1ozZmkHSXx+7Tq3c9a3VY5ESWHB5sHOn/sbREGqPcHnHzepAhaXKDvcymEmsQzCLNAtQV0d2jw97Q7qhA8="}
